@page "/"

<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-10">

    <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold text-blue-600">
        Tailwind CSS 4.3 with ASP.NET Maui
    </h1>

    <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-gray-700">
        This page explains how to set up Tailwind CSS version 4.3
        with the CLI and PostCSS in an ASP.NET Core Razor Pages project.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
            1. Install dependencies
        </h2>

        <p class="mb-3">
            Initialize Node.js in your project:
        </p>

        <pre class="rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

npm init -y
</pre>

        <p class="mt-4 mb-3">
            Install Tailwind CSS 4.3, the CLI, and PostCSS:
        </p>

        <pre class="rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

npm install tailwindcss@latest tailwindcss/cli tailwindcss/postcss postcss postcss-cli --save-dev
</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
            2. Tailwind CSS source file
        </h2>

        <p>
            With Tailwind CSS 4, the CSS entry file uses the new syntax:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

    import "tailwindcss";
</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
            3. Configure PostCSS
        </h2>

        <p>
            Create the file <strong>postcss.config.mjs</strong>:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

export default {
plugins: {
"tailwindcss/postcss": {},
},
};
</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
            4. Build Tailwind CSS
        </h2>

        <p>
            Add the following scripts to <strong>package.json</strong>:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

"scripts": {
"build": "npx tailwindcss/cli -i ./Styles/app.css -o ./wwwroot/css/site.css",
"watch": "npx tailwindcss/cli -i ./Styles/app.css -o ./wwwroot/css/site.css --watch"
}
</pre>

        <p class="mt-4">
            Build the CSS file:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

npm run build
</pre>

        <p class="mt-4">
            Run Tailwind in watch mode during development:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

npm run watch
</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
            5. Use Tailwind in Razor Pages
        </h2>

        <p>
            Reference the generated CSS file in
            <strong>_Layout.cshtml</strong>:
        </p>

        <pre class="mt-3 rounded bg-gray-900 p-4 text-white">

<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/site.css" asp-append-version="true" />
</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded bg-blue-50 p-6">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-700">
            Tailwind Example
        </h2>

        <button class="rounded bg-blue-600 px-5 py-2 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-700">
            Tailwind 4.3 Button
        </button>

        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">
            If this button appears with a blue background and a hover effect,
            Tailwind CSS is correctly configured in your Razor Pages project.
        </p>
    </section>

</div>


